# Quality Gate Architecture — Single Source of Truth

## Structure

```
unified-trading-pm/scripts/quality-gates-base/
├── base-service.sh   # Gate logic for 28 service repos (FastAPI apps, workers, APIs)
├── base-library.sh   # Gate logic for 17 library/interface repos
└── base-codex.sh     # Gate logic for docs-only repos (no Python source)
```

Per-repo `scripts/quality-gates.sh` is a ~10-line config stub. It only sets:
`SERVICE_NAME / PACKAGE_NAME`, `SOURCE_DIR`, `MIN_COVERAGE`, `RUN_INTEGRATION`, `LOCAL_DEPS`
then sources the appropriate base: `source "${WORKSPACE_ROOT}/unified-trading-pm/scripts/quality-gates-base/base-service.sh"`

Scaffold templates (used by rollout to write stubs to new repos — not gate logic):
- `unified-trading-codex/06-coding-standards/quality-gates-service-template.sh`
- `unified-trading-codex/06-coding-standards/quality-gates-library-template.sh`

## Rules

RULE: NEVER edit gate logic in a per-repo `scripts/quality-gates.sh`. It is a config stub only.
NEVER: Copy gate logic from a base script into a per-repo file.
WHY: The base scripts in PM are the SSOT. One edit in PM fixes all 47 repos instantly — no rollout needed.

## When to edit what

| Change type | Where to edit | Propagation? |
|---|---|---|
| New gate check, modified logic, new compliance step | PM `scripts/quality-gates-base/base-{service,library,codex}.sh` | None — all repos source live |
| New required stub variable (interface change) | Codex scaffold template → run rollout → commit stubs | Yes — rollout writes stubs |
| Per-repo config (MIN_COVERAGE, LOCAL_DEPS, RUN_INTEGRATION) | The per-repo `scripts/quality-gates.sh` stub only | None |
| Documented repo exception | `QUALITY_GATE_BYPASS_AUDIT.md` in that repo | None |

## Stub interface change protocol (rare — only when base script adds a NEW required variable)

1. Add new variable with default to base script first (non-breaking — stubs not required to set it)
2. If stubs MUST set it:
   a. Edit the codex scaffold template to include the new variable
   b. `python3 unified-trading-pm/scripts/propagation/rollout-quality-gates-unified.py --dry-run`
   c. `python3 unified-trading-pm/scripts/propagation/rollout-quality-gates-unified.py`
   d. Commit updated stubs in each affected repo
   e. Bump `REQUIRED_BASE_VERSION` in the base script

